ull,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.3105987248324297,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.11160113853179444,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.13245,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":88.3,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Firefly Aerospace Inc. operates as a space and defense technology company and provides mission solutions for national security, government, and commercial customers in United States. The company offers integrated launch and space services technology that is committed to enabling launch, transit, and operations in space. It also provides Launch solutions, such as Alpha, a responsive launch services; and Eclipse, a medium-lift launch vehicles. In addition, the company offers spacecraft solutions platforms, including Blue Ghost, a lunar delivery and operation service; and Elytra, which provides space maneuverability and servicing. Further, it provides software and sensor solutions; national security software and big data processing capabilities; and responsive space services, as well as Ocula, a lunar imaging service. Firefly Aerospace Inc. was incorporated in 2017 and is headquartered in Leander, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jason  Kim | CEO & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $113K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers. Stock-based compensation of $13K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Firefly Aerospace Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $3.0B market cap on $160M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at -78% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 19% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $238M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -16.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 31.1% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 11% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 13% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Industrials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 172% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 177% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why Firefly Aerospace Stock Dropped on Friday","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/why-firefly-aerospace-stock-dropped-182511000.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795199763.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Firefly Aerospace Stock Dropped This Week","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/why-firefly-aerospace-stock-dropped-112302000.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795174095.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.153,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Firefly Aerospace CEO Kim Jesung Awarded 3,472 RSUs Under 2025 Incentive Plan","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/firefly-aerospace-ceo-kim-jesung-awarded-3472-rsus-under-2025-incentive-plan","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795141488.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.637,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Firefly Aerospace CFO Darren Ma Granted 2,916 RSUs Under 2025 Incentive Plan","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/firefly-aerospace-cfo-darren-ma-granted-2916-rsus-under-2025-incentive-plan","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795046806.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.542,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Firefly Aerospace CFO Remington Wu Acquires 2,145 RSUs Under 2025 Omnibus Incentive Plan","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/fir